-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lib_plain_lib.pcpp - Build kind: a lib that does not use the runtime (dep)

  A `module lib` is a static library. This one's code never calls into the
  PaskalCPP runtime (no div / mod, guard, raise, sets, ...), so its build
  is the lib alone: no startup hook, no pcpp_runtime beside it from this
  build. lib_plain links it from PaskalCPP; a C program built by another
  toolchain links it with a plain C driver (the lib area's code test).
  lib_runtime_lib is the other case.
*******************************************************************************/

module lib lib_plain_lib;

/*
  @@test
    kind dep
  @@end
*/

exported routine clink lib_plain_lib_add(AA: int32; AB: int32): int32;
begin
  return AA + AB;
end;

end.
